# Project Context
- Target platform: ESP32-C3 with HomeSpan (Arduino framework)
- Device runs 24/7 unattended – stability takes priority over elegance and feature scope

# Response Behavior
- Respond to the user in German
- Keep explanations short and concrete; code comments in German
- For every proposed change: briefly justify why it is memory- and runtime-safe
- Never silently rewrite unrelated code – only touch what the task requires

# General Principles
- Take compiler warnings seriously – code must compile warning-free
- Constants instead of magic numbers (prefer `constexpr`, `#define` only for legacy compatibility)
- Meaningful variable names, no cryptic abbreviations
- Prefer simple, proven solutions over clever ones
